{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-12T16:08:56.108Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"72bc6070cdf8e143b3ffadf4","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-ziv9yb"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Identity refusal reads only top-level fields, so a runtime field mapped onto comments, notes, learnings or dependencies can store a nested author with URL userinfo"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Found by the CodeRabbit review of PR 1712 (pm-gh1707). assertIdentityFieldsWithoutUrlCredentials checks the top-level author, assignee and claim_principal of create metadata and runtime update values. A runtime field definition may set metadata_key to a built-in collection such as comments, notes, learnings or dependencies, and an array field without a value_schema stores its JSON as-is, so a nested entry's author can carry URL userinfo past the guard. Fix: walk nested arrays and objects of the checked values (bounded depth) for identity keys, or reject built-in collection keys as runtime metadata_key during field normalization."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["identity","redaction","runtime-fields","security"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-12T16:08:56.108Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-12T16:08:56.108Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":45},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A runtime or registered field value whose nested entries carry an author, assignee or claim_principal with URL userinfo is refused like a top-level one; Ordinary nested collections without credentials are unaffected; A regression test covers a runtime array field mapped onto comments"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-qwoy"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"No field path can store an identity carrying URL userinfo"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Nested authors in runtime collection fields bypass the identity refusal"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1707","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-12T16:08:56.108Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"8e378d070bdcdf24fbe5b00a4afa73f559b73c395428e6796ca339f80a9c1b57","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"38e103917c6a6c698961fc702c5e1de0125d615b90c8d3f4b6e8322ce323515c"}
